# COMMITTEE#1 — CLAIM-0071 (PROJ-0041, IMMATURE-WEDGE: databases-and-storage-engines — fjall LSM journal recovery)
## EMPIRICAL CROSS-AREA PHENOMENON, effect=SUPPORT (orchestrator-recovered from on-node results; researcher wedged then self-recovered; work verified real, no fabrication). Vote HONESTLY by role. Real 6/6 by role; committee#1 = gate to L1 or converge.

## ★★★ THE #1 STRESS-TEST (orchestrator flags FRONT-AND-CENTER — the two killers this claim must beat):
A. GATE-4 FOLKLORE: a reviewer will say "single-file WALs losing data after a hole/torn write is known." THE DECISIVE QUESTION: is the contribution genuinely above that? It is NOT "WALs lose data." It is the LOUD-vs-SILENT recovery ASYMMETRY by corruption LOCATION under the DEFAULT durability mode: in-DATA corruption -> loud Err(ChecksumMismatch) (the per-batch xxh3 guards only the in-data case); FRAMING corruption (torn/missing-End/lost-Start) -> silent truncate_to(last_valid_pos)+return None, recovery loop ends NORMALLY, DB OPENS CLEAN with NO Err, discarding committed data EVEN PHYSICALLY PRESENT AFTER THE HOLE. fjall-specific, source-verified, un-owned (#53 = cosmetic trailing-batch warning; #112/#113 = a DIFFERENT fixed clean-path bug; no CVE/Jepsen/paper). Is the location-asymmetry + clean-open a genuine publishable finding (SUPPORT) or folklore-dressed-up (YELLOW/RED)?
B. ★ THE DURABILITY-CONTRACT BOUNDARY (the honest L1 gap — judge whether it caps this): the silent-loss is demonstrated for FRAMING corruption + for a real dm-flakey dropped-WRITEBACK crash of UN-fsync'd Buffer-mode data (documented loss) + a faithful labeled reorder-SIM that discards acked data present after an interior hole. NOT yet achieved: a REAL reordered DEVICE write dropping data whose SyncAll fsync ALREADY COMPLETED (dm-log-writes barrier-reorder replay / power-cut crossing an unhonored fsync barrier). So the claim's teeth depend on: does fjall's framing-desync recovery silently drop data that was ACKNOWLEDGED-DURABLE (SyncAll returned Ok), or only in-flight/post-ack-pre-durable data? The committee must decide if the demonstrated form (framing corruption + dropped-writeback + faithful sim on real journal bytes) is sufficient, or if GREEN requires the real post-fsync reordered-write (L1).

## CLAIM
In fjall 3.1.4 (young Rust LSM embedded KV; real adoption brk/atproto; no Jepsen/CVE/paper), journal FRAMING corruption (default PersistMode::Buffer's natural crash signature) is silently treated as an incomplete trailing batch -> DB opens with NO error while discarding committed data after the corruption point, WHEREAS in-DATA corruption (same byte budget) is caught by xxh3 checksum and surfaced as a loud Err. WHERE the corruption lands, not how much, decides loud-fail vs silent-loss. NULL EXIT: open fails loudly OR all keys present on framing corruption -> did NOT happen (triggered only on the in-data control).

## L0 RESULT (EXP-0084; cli:devvm14382; pinned fjall =3.1.4 / lsm-tree 3.1.4 / Rust 1.96.0; root)
SOURCE-VERIFIED (installed 3.1.4 journal/): default PersistMode::Buffer = literal no-op (writer.rs:232, no fsync). Recovery routes by LOCATION: SILENT framing-desync -> truncate_to(last_valid_pos)+return None, logged only debug/trace ("missing terminator... discarding to keep atomicity"), recovery loop ends normally -> clean open no Err. LOUD in-data -> End-marker got_checksum != expected -> ERROR + Err(JournalRecovery(ChecksumMismatch)). Distinct from FIXED #112/#113.
ASYMMETRY TABLE (50 keys, each db.persist(SyncAll)->Ok, corrupt journal, reopen): data_flip DATA (CONTROL) -> open_ok=FALSE, 0/50, LOUD ChecksumMismatch. trailing framing -> true, 49/50, none. mid_truncate -> true, 25/50, SILENT. mid_zero -> true, 16/50, SILENT. mid_flip -> true, 25/50, SILENT. early_trunc -> true, 2/50, SILENT. In-data control LOUD; all 5 framing modes open clean 0<keys<50 no error. NULL triggered ONLY on the control (as predicted). IT-MATTERS met.
★ REAL-CRASH HARNESS: (a) dm-flakey v1.5.0 root device-level dropped-writeback crash (loop-backed ext4, drop_writes drops dirty journal-page writeback): OPEN_OK=true ERR=none silent loss (Case A 5/50; Case B data-already-in-SST 50/50 correct). HONEST LIMIT: dm-flakey only drops UN-fsync'd Buffer data (documented loss); cannot drop post-SyncAll-fsync-completed data. (b) FAITHFUL labeled reorder-SIM on the REAL fjall journal bytes (zero one interior 4KiB page = a dropped page-writeback, later acked batches intact): drop_page=1 -> OPEN_OK=true, 38/50, ERR=none -> 12 SyncAll-acked keys physically present after the hole SILENTLY discarded; recovery log debug-level "truncating/missing terminator/discarding" then clean open.

## NOVELTY / PRIOR-ART: not folklore "WALs lose data after a hole." The loud-vs-silent-by-LOCATION asymmetry + clean-open-while-discarding-data-present-after-the-hole is fjall-specific + source-verified + un-owned (#53 cosmetic trailing; #112/#113 different fixed bug; no CVE/Jepsen/paper). Committee scrutinize: is there a fjall issue / LSM-recovery paper that owns the LOCATION-asymmetry? (If yes -> RED.)

## ORCHESTRATOR NOTE (NOT advocacy; this claim was orchestrator-RECOVERED from a wedged researcher — work file-transferred + verified real, no fabrication): clean L0 (source-verified mechanism, in-data control held LOUD as the discriminator, real dm-flakey root crash + faithful reorder-sim). The make-or-break is the durability-contract boundary (stress-test B): does the silent recovery drop ACKNOWLEDGED-DURABLE (post-SyncAll-fsync) data, or only in-flight/post-ack-pre-durable? If the demonstrated form is a genuine silent-acked-loss finding -> advance to an L1 (dm-log-writes barrier-reorder replay to drop post-fsush-completed data) toward green. If the silent loss is only for un-fsync'd Buffer data (= documented PersistMode::Buffer behavior) -> the location-asymmetry + clean-open is still novel but the severity caps lower -> YELLOW. Judge honestly. Real 6/6 by role. Prompt version v003.
